# Secrets — NEVER commit. Stage locally before `railway up`.
# (Only the two key files are secret; overlay/config-store/ is plain ForceImport config and IS tracked.)
overlay/pf.jwk
overlay/pingfederate-system-keys.xml
*.lic

# Build outputs / config artifact — staged into the context, not versioned here.
#   *.war, *.jar         <- `mvn -q package` outputs of this repo (modules/ via build/stage-modules.sh)
#   data*.zip            <- terraform/ Phase-2 configArchive export. A PF config archive is a PLAIN
#                           ZIP that CONTAINS pf.jwk (the master key), pingfederate-system-keys.xml,
#                           both keystores, the admin password hash and master-key-reversible client
#                           secrets. It is a SECRET, never a versionable artifact — the earlier
#                           "encrypted with pf.jwk so it is safe to commit" reading was wrong, and the
#                           narrow `data.zip` pattern below is exactly how data.staging.zip got in.
*.war
*.jar
data*.zip
